### 4. Core Mechanical Takeaways & Policy Insights

1. **The Generalization Ceiling vs. Specialized Adaptation:**
As observed across the 7-Rider matrix, while specific targeted heuristics can solve individual archetype setups (e.g., locking execution charge against V3 or aggressive turtling against X), a **generalized neural policy (`state256-action17`) faces inherent trade-offs when evaluated across diverse playstyles**. Optimizing policy weights for high-damage payload conversion against brawlers (Nigo/Mirror) naturally leaves friction against high-mobility evasive kits (Amazon).
2. **Chi Surplus & Stance Efficiency:**
Across all passing matchups (Ichigo, Nigo, V3, Riderman, X, Stronger), maintaining a positive Chi Net Advantage (**+0.30 to +4.37 NetAdv**) and capping defensive `A`-guard usage below 15% directly correlated with win rate stability.
3. **Execution Charge Calibration:**
An average execution charge target of **~61.5%–63.5%** proved optimal for physical priority generation (42.5%–54.7% WR) in 6 out of 7 matchups, only falling short when opponent speed modifiers out-scale charge startup frames.

